  "id": "COMPOUND:18046 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Caesalpiniaphenol B appears to interact with DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular targets, as evidenced by its relationship with SCCH-26, CHP-134, and MOVP-3. These entities are all implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the inhibition of DNA synthesis or the modulation of DNA replication processes. The final scores from the paths indicate a consistent level of confidence in the relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets implies that Caesalpiniaphenol B may act through a complex network of molecular pathways, potentially influencing DNA polymerase iota in multiple ways. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Caesalpiniaphenol B and DNA polymerase iota, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mode of action and the biological relevance of these interactions.",
